    {
      "id": "post-3",
      "author": {
        "id": "interviewer-elena",
        "name": "Dr. Elena Rostova",
        "headline": "Principal Systems Architect at Nimbus Technologies",
        "role": "INTERVIEWER",
        "company": "Nimbus Technologies"
      },
      "content": "💡 Technical Interview Tip for 2026:\n\nWhen a senior interviewer asks you to design a high-throughput system, resist the urge to immediately say 'I will add Redis and Kafka'.\n\nInstead:\n1. Ask for SLA requirements: read vs write ratio, latency target, and consistency needs (p99 vs p50).\n2. Calculate back-of-the-envelope storage and bandwidth.\n3. Identify the true bottleneck before choosing tools.\n\nWhat is your biggest hurdle in technical interviews right now?",
      "category": "Career Advice",
      "tags": [
        "CareerAdvice",
        "SystemDesign",
        "InterviewTips",
        "Engineering"
      ],
      "poll": {
        "id": "poll-elena-1",
